CAL Unknown  ? ?  ?   ? 4 
;THE CALCIUM ION IS COORDINATED TO THE TWO CARBOXYLATE OXYGENS OF ASP 49 AND EACH CARBONYL OXYGENS OF TYR 28, GLY 30 AND GLY 32 AS WELL AS TWO WATER MOLECULES (HOH 212 AND HOH 213). THESE LIGAND ATOMS FORM A DISTORTED PENTAGONAL BIPYRAMID STRUCTURE. THE AVERAGE DISTANCE OF CALCIUM ION TO LIGANDS OF PROTEIN OXYGEN IS 2.4 ANGSTROMS.
;
AC1 Software A CA 200 ? 5 'BINDING SITE FOR RESIDUE CA A 200' 
